  "interpretive_boundary": "The matched-additive reference gives an exact Shapley allocation of the observed full-shunt-versus-additive localization contrast, but it is not a literal no-factor factorial corner. The unperturbed-reference result is the conventional factorial sensitivity. Both operate on the nonlinear localization-index payoff. Adjoint-only and driving-force-only states are algebraic substitutions in the passive model, not independent biological interventions or evidence of in vivo plasticity.",
